From 4ae9c9b7808881bcf81f23ab01af02284173d6be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: netplay <netplay@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:49:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Netplay: both Game Boys in gb2p_machine, shared clock
 enable

The two cores, the link cable and the clock enables move from Gameboy.sv
into rtl/gb2p_machine.sv. speedcontrol_shared.sv drives both cores from one
divider: the enables are skipped while either core's ROM read waits for the
SDRAM, while hold is 1 or while pausevideo is 1, so SDRAM latency never
changes the order of events between the two cores (SPEC 11.1). Gameboy.sv
selects it (shared_ce = 1); shared_ce = 0 gives the upstream per-core
enables. The cart RTC can count emulated cycles instead of wall-clock time
(rtc_emu, 0 in Gameboy.sv for now).
